WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.602 --> 00:00:02.320
- Football, marriage.

00:00:02.320 --> 00:00:04.224
Two forces that have been in opposition

00:00:04.224 --> 00:00:05.849
since the beginning of time.

00:00:05.849 --> 00:00:08.840
Today we have a man,
Ned, and his wife, Ariel.

00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:12.125
And we're going to find out do
you know your favorite thing

00:00:12.125 --> 00:00:13.542
more than you know your wife?

00:00:13.542 --> 00:00:15.598
(thunder)
I hope he does

00:00:15.598 --> 00:00:17.861
or else he'll be in
trouble and I'll laugh.

00:00:17.861 --> 00:00:22.754
(playfully dramatic music)

00:00:23.223 --> 00:00:24.896
Alright Ned, we're gonna talk football,

00:00:24.896 --> 00:00:26.382
we're gonna talk your
wife, you ready for this?

00:00:26.382 --> 00:00:27.821
- Yeah, baby, let's do this.

00:00:27.821 --> 00:00:28.657
- Do you know football?

00:00:28.657 --> 00:00:29.458
- Yes.

00:00:29.458 --> 00:00:30.758
- Do you know your wife?
- [Ned] More.

00:00:30.758 --> 00:00:32.420
- Ariel, how are you feeling today?

00:00:32.420 --> 00:00:35.565
He's gonna get more
questions right about me

00:00:35.565 --> 00:00:37.097
than he is about football.

00:00:37.097 --> 00:00:38.699
- One, two, three are you feeling ready?

00:00:38.699 --> 00:00:40.417
- [Ned] Yes!
- Oh yeah, yeah baby!

00:00:40.417 --> 00:00:41.938
Yeah, psych me up.
- [Ned] Yeah, what's up?

00:00:41.938 --> 00:00:42.990
- Alright, question number one,

00:00:42.990 --> 00:00:46.728
Ned, name five offensive
positions in the NFL.

00:00:46.728 --> 00:00:48.469
- Quarterback, running
back, wide receiver,

00:00:48.469 --> 00:00:50.129
offensive tackle, tight end.

00:00:50.129 --> 00:00:52.532
- Ned, name five of
Ariel's favorite foods.

00:00:52.532 --> 00:00:54.890
- Um, uh let's see.

00:00:54.890 --> 00:00:59.890
- So olives, breakfast burritos,

00:00:59.997 --> 00:01:01.970
- [Host] Not on my list
but I'll let it slide.

00:01:01.970 --> 00:01:04.571
- pasta, salad,

00:01:04.571 --> 00:01:05.732
- You need one more Ned.

00:01:05.732 --> 00:01:07.136
- [Ned] Uh,
- Remember this is

00:01:07.136 --> 00:01:09.309
the easiest question that
we have in this stack,

00:01:09.309 --> 00:01:10.515
so take your time.

00:01:10.515 --> 00:01:12.048
- How 'bout, how 'bout like a dessert?

00:01:12.048 --> 00:01:13.012
- Oh Tiramisu.

00:01:13.012 --> 00:01:14.254
- Alright.

00:01:15.344 --> 00:01:17.060
How many minutes are in a football game?

00:01:17.060 --> 00:01:19.406
- Uh, 60 minutes.

00:01:19.406 --> 00:01:21.821
- How long does it take Ariel
to get ready in the morning?

00:01:21.821 --> 00:01:22.865
- About 45 minutes.

00:01:22.865 --> 00:01:24.641
- 20 minutes max.

00:01:24.641 --> 00:01:25.860
- That is not true,
(laughing)

00:01:25.860 --> 00:01:27.358
that is not true!

00:01:27.358 --> 00:01:28.565
- Sorry, we're gonna have to

00:01:28.565 --> 00:01:30.585
give you a big red X on that one.

00:01:30.585 --> 00:01:32.082
Alright Ned you've got 20 seconds,

00:01:32.082 --> 00:01:35.008
name as many starting quarter
backs in the NFL as possible.

00:01:35.008 --> 00:01:36.227
Ready, set, go!

00:01:36.227 --> 00:01:38.909
Blake Bortles, Tom Brady, Russell Wilson,

00:01:38.909 --> 00:01:41.243
Colin Kaepernick, Phillip Rivers,

00:01:41.243 --> 00:01:44.865
Ryan Fitzpatrick, Cam
Newton, Matthew Stafford.

00:01:44.865 --> 00:01:46.386
- Alright, now you have 10 seconds,

00:01:46.386 --> 00:01:48.870
name as many as Ariel's
bridal party as you can.

00:01:48.870 --> 00:01:49.961
Ready, set, go!

00:01:49.961 --> 00:01:52.643
Oh, Danielle, Carol, Becca,

00:01:52.643 --> 00:01:54.605
Annelise, Grace.

00:01:54.605 --> 00:01:55.627
Five for five.

00:01:55.627 --> 00:01:57.542
Oh, you can't phase me, Zack.

00:01:57.542 --> 00:01:58.866
I'm cold as ice.

00:01:58.866 --> 00:02:00.921
Ned, name the last two players

00:02:00.921 --> 00:02:02.870
featured on the Madden NFL cover.

00:02:02.870 --> 00:02:05.308
This past year was Odell Beckham Jr.

00:02:05.308 --> 00:02:07.921
and the year before that
it was Richard Sherman,

00:02:07.921 --> 00:02:10.661
but more accurately the
entire Seattle Seahawks.

00:02:10.661 --> 00:02:14.562
- Describe Ariel's last
profile picture on Facebook.

00:02:14.562 --> 00:02:18.378
I remember the one when
we first met really well.

00:02:18.378 --> 00:02:20.990
It was her and a giant dog named George.

00:02:20.990 --> 00:02:22.395
- Not the question.

00:02:22.395 --> 00:02:23.591
- Not the question, okay.

00:02:23.591 --> 00:02:24.392
(laughing)

00:02:24.392 --> 00:02:26.958
I think it was one from our wedding

00:02:26.958 --> 00:02:29.291
when she was like looking at me.

00:02:29.291 --> 00:02:30.231
- You're sweating man.

00:02:30.231 --> 00:02:32.275
- You guys totally
debowed my emotional story

00:02:32.275 --> 00:02:33.772
about our first meeting.

00:02:33.772 --> 00:02:37.010
(laughing)
- I'm sorry.

00:02:37.010 --> 00:02:39.600
- How many Super Bowl
rings does Tom Brady have?

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:41.597
- [Ned] Two.
- Four.

00:02:41.597 --> 00:02:42.874
- Four?
- [Host] Yes.

00:02:42.874 --> 00:02:44.674
- (groans) I hate Tom Brady.

00:02:44.674 --> 00:02:45.916
Four Super Bowl rings?

00:02:45.916 --> 00:02:48.098
- Four. How many rings
does Ariel normally wear?

00:02:48.098 --> 00:02:50.343
- Uh two, she wears her engagement ring

00:02:50.343 --> 00:02:52.137
and her wedding ring.

00:02:52.561 --> 00:02:54.906
- How many times have the
Jaguars made the playoffs?

00:02:54.906 --> 00:02:57.787
- (sighs) That's hard.

00:02:58.198 --> 00:02:59.615
1996.

00:02:59.615 --> 00:03:04.589
(voice in fast forward)

00:03:08.914 --> 00:03:09.854
- [Host] So your answer?

00:03:09.854 --> 00:03:11.317
- I'm gonna go with six.

00:03:11.317 --> 00:03:13.314
- That is (censor beep) impressive.

00:03:13.314 --> 00:03:15.218
Not only do you have, you got the number,

00:03:15.218 --> 00:03:16.472
you got the years!

00:03:16.472 --> 00:03:19.618
- How many times has Ariel
been to a black tie event?

00:03:19.618 --> 00:03:22.218
- Uh, that's pretty tough.

00:03:22.218 --> 00:03:25.120
We went to one wedding this year.

00:03:25.120 --> 00:03:28.008
(voice in fast forward)

00:03:28.008 --> 00:03:30.028
I'll say seven.

00:03:30.028 --> 00:03:31.490
- What did I say?

00:03:31.490 --> 00:03:32.803
- (censor beep) this.

00:03:32.803 --> 00:03:33.848
That is correct.

00:03:33.848 --> 00:03:36.088
- What year did the Jaguars join the NFL?

00:03:36.088 --> 00:03:37.261
- I'm gonna go with 1995

00:03:37.261 --> 00:03:39.107
'cause that's when the
official announcement was.

00:03:39.107 --> 00:03:41.797
- What year did Ariel
get her first computer?

00:03:42.437 --> 00:03:47.270
- I will say, 2000 and three.

00:03:48.526 --> 00:03:49.885
- That is correct.

00:03:49.885 --> 00:03:52.177
- Oh my God, yes!

00:03:52.926 --> 00:03:55.005
Ned, I'm frustrated to report

00:03:55.005 --> 00:03:57.546
that you do know your wife
as well as you know football.

00:03:57.546 --> 00:03:59.904
So there you go, turns
out Ned knows as much

00:03:59.904 --> 00:04:01.564
about his wife as he does the NFL.

00:04:01.564 --> 00:04:03.606
Pretty adorable, also
a little frustrating.

00:04:03.606 --> 00:04:04.721
Thanks for watching

00:04:04.721 --> 00:04:06.846
"Do you know your partner better
than your favorite thing?"

00:04:06.846 --> 00:04:08.622
I'm Zack, see ya next time.

00:04:08.622 --> 00:04:13.354
(playfully dramatic music)

